Study Buddy – Student Planner 
Project Brief – Team 18 
Due Date: Week 7 

 

Overview of the Project 

Study Buddy is a lightweight student planner designed to help students manage their time, stay motivated, and feel more in control of their academic responsibilities. The idea came from our shared experiences as students as we are constantly juggling deadlines, part-time jobs, and other commitments while trying to stay focused. We wanted to create something that’s actually useful and not another complicated app that no one ends up using. Our goal is to keep it simple, practical, and student friendly. 

Study Buddy includes four core features: 

Daily To-Do Card System – to keep track of day-to-day study goals. 
Weekly Timetable Builder – to help students map out their schedules visually. 
Motivational Quotes or Countdown Page – to stay inspired and focused. 
Pomodoro Timer – to encourage better time management through short, focused bursts of study. 
Team Persona Allocations 

To make sure everyone in the group is working with a different user scenario, here’s how we’ve divided the personas: 

Suraiya Supti – Nina: Full-time student juggling work, study, and volunteering. 
Sovanndevid Nong – Toby: A social learner who prefers study groups. 
Shovana Shrestha – Amira: A mature-aged student studying online while raising children. 
Manjil Bolakhe – Leo: A neurodiverse student who needs structure, simplicity, and visual aids. 
Suraiya’s Assigned Persona: Nina 

Nina is a full-time university student who also works part-time at a local café and volunteers on weekends. She’s highly motivated, but often overwhelmed. Her biggest challenges are staying on top of deadlines and finding time for everything. She doesn’t want anything too fancy or complex, just something that’s easy to use, helps her stay organised, and keeps her calm. 

User Hypothesis for Nina 

We believe that if Nina can easily plan her weekly schedule and track her daily tasks, she’ll feel less anxious and more in control of her studies. Visual tools like colour-coded timetables, checklists, and countdowns will make a real difference for someone like her. 

Testing Nina’s Experience 

To test whether our solution works for Nina, we’ll ask users like her to: 

Create a weekly timetable and see if it takes less than 2 minutes. 
Add tasks to the to-do list and check them off throughout the day. 
See if the countdown/motivational quotes help them feel more focused or encouraged. 
Devid’s Assigned Persona: Toby 

Toby is a sociable university individual in his second semester in Bachelor of Compute Science. He keens in group learning environments and often the study organiser for him and his peers. His biggest struggle is dealing with not just personal but also group deadline, especially when balancing multiple group assignments and other commitments. Toby values and wanted quick communication and collaboration tools where it easy for him to coordinate study session, track assigned task and overall keeping every member accountable. 

 

 

User Hypothesis for Toby 

Our assumption is that if Toby was provided a tool that enable him to efficiently managed study session while keep tracks of any shared tasks with his peers, he will likely become more productive and avoid missing important deadline. Collaborative features like shared timetable with the ability to keep tracks of any necessary to do list, peer reminders and study session RSVP will help boost the overall engagement and strengthen group accountability. 

Testing Toby’s Experience 

To assess and validate our assumptions about Toby, we will ask users like him to :  

Create and manage a share group timetable to RSVP study session. 
Use a collaborative to do list to assign and tracks group tasks. 
User peer reminder for task follow-ups and group accountability. 
Shovana’s Assigned Persona: Amira 

Amira is a mature-aged student who studies online while also taking care of her children. Her daily routine is busy and unpredictable, filled with parenting responsibilities, housework, and study sessions squeezed into short, quiet moments. Amira is motivated to complete her degree but often feels overwhelmed trying to juggle everything. Her biggest challenges are staying on top of tasks and managing her time effectively. She prefers something simple and easy to use that doesn't take up too much of her limited time. 

User Hypothesis for Amira 

We believe that if Amira is given a tool that allows her to manage daily tasks in a quick and flexible way, she will feel more in control and less overwhelmed. Features such as a straightforward to-do list, a Pomodoro timer, and motivational messages will help her stay productive and encouraged even on her busiest days. 

 

 

Testing Amira’s Experience 

To test whether our solution supports Amira’s needs, we will ask users like her to: 

Add and check off tasks from a daily to-do list. 
Use a Pomodoro timer to complete a short study session. 
Read a motivational quote or message and reflect on how it affects their mindset. 
 

